{"number":59,"title":"Canon patch (blocked on push scope): executor-routine fixes for #53–#57","body":"The canon changes for #53, #54, #55, #56 and #57 are complete and tested — but **this session cannot push them**. The git proxy returns `403` for `missingbulb/Claudinite`; the session&#39;s GitHub scope is `missingbulb/claudinitewebsite` alone. That&#39;s an organization egress policy, which the proxy README says to report rather than route around.

So the work is preserved here, to be applied from a session whose environment includes the canon repo.

**Local commit:** `40f316c` — *Stop the executor routine tripping over its own conformance checks* (8 files, +273 / −12)

**Verified before this was written:**
- full canon suite — `1148 pass / 0 fail`
- `node engine/checks/check_the_world.mjs` — 0 blocking (9 advisories, all pre-existing on `main`, unchanged by this diff)
- every new test confirmed to **fail against the unmodified source first**, then pass
- the new `conformance-workflow` rule run against this repo&#39;s real `ci.yml`: 1 finding before the fix, 0 after

## To apply

```sh
git checkout -b claude/executor-routine-fixes
git apply canon-executor-fixes.patch
```

## Patch


<code>git diff main..HEAD</code>

